# TypeScript package rules

- Read `.agents/skills/css-doctor-integrations/SKILL.md` when touching CLI,
  Vite, or Next; read `css-doctor-binding` for NAPI changes.
- ESM + strict TS + tsup. Tests run with `tsx --test`.
- FE scope: use `type` for all object definitions; do not use `interface`.
  Generated NAPI `*.d.ts` is the only exception.
- Preserve public option/diagnostic interfaces; check generated `.d.ts`.
- NAPI boundary uses `f64` for ratios and `u32` for indices/counters.
- Integration plugins must contain parse/split/callback/reporter failures.
- Do not mutate user configs destructively; preserve original webpack hooks and
  plugin arrays.
- Build binding before typechecking consumers; generated binding d.ts is ignored
  by git and must be regenerated locally.
- Verify: `pnpm --filter <pkg> typecheck`, `build`, `test`.
